    },
    "claim": {
      "claim_id": "P22-E1-12",
      "paper_locator": "manuscript.tex:L310-L320",
      "selection_tier": "HIGH-IMPACT",
      "text": "It is essential that \\(\\omega\\) is an epimorphism \\emph{in the category of\nsheaves}.  For sheaves of abelian groups, this means that a target section\nhas preimages after passage to a cover.  It does not mean that\n\\[\n \\Zsh(U)\\longrightarrow\\Wsh(U)\n\\]\nis surjective for every object \\(U\\).  Equivalently, the cokernel sheaf\nvanishes even though an objectwise cokernel presheaf can have nonzero\nsections before sheafification; see the local exactness criterion in\n\\cite[Tag 03CN]{StacksProject}.  The distinction is precisely what permits\na local factorization of \\(1-xT^N\\) while obstructing its descent."
    },
    "content_handling": {
      "contains_external_text": true,
      "rights_basis": "not_assessed",
      "sharing_scope": "session_only"
    },
    "detail": "Tag 03CN supports cokernel sheafification and local rather than objectwise surjectivity.",
    "excerpt": {
      "captured_at": "2026-08-24T13:02:37Z",
      "excerpt_sha256": "c8ec2684dcd019a3e3a20fee6ffa6b4b4bbdd3fcddda64b8f238fdb388cfe323",
      "source_span_utf8": {
        "end": 143,
        "start": 0
      },
      "state": "agent_extracted",
      "text": "The cokernel $\\mathop{\\mathrm{Coker}}(\\varphi )$ of $\\varphi $ is the sheafification of the cokernel of $\\varphi $ as a morphism of presheaves."
    },
